description:
`Boolean(x)` is a standard AS2 type-cast function. In AVM1 there is no dedicated ActionToBoolean opcode, but the correct emulation is: push x, then use a double-not (`ActionNot` twice) to coerce to a proper boolean value.

**Current state:**
`Number(x)` is special-cased in `compiler.ts` at line 2265 (emits ActionToNumber 0x4A) and `String(x)` at line 2272 (emits ActionToString 0x4B). There is no corresponding special case for `Boolean(x)`.

Without a special case, `Boolean(x)` falls through to the generic `ActionCallFunction` path which pushes the string `"Boolean"` and calls it. In AVM1/Flash 8 there is no built-in global `Boolean` function callable this way, so this will produce `undefined` at runtime instead of a boolean coercion.

**Fix needed** in `compiler.ts` `compileCallExpr()`:
```ts
// Built-in: Boolean(x) → push x, ActionNot, ActionNot (double-not coerces to boolean)
if (name === 'Boolean' && expr.args.length === 1) {
  this.compileExpr(expr.args[0]!);
  this.emit(0x12); // ActionNot
  this.emit(0x12); // ActionNot
  return;
}
```
Also add `Boolean` to the exclusion list in `collectStrings()` (same pattern as `Number` and `String` on lines 330–331).
